{
 "id": "lem-sfb-profinite-field-scalar-annihilator-hull",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Rank-one continuous field annihilator sheaves in the finite-model hull",
 "statement": "Work in the small-site and indexing universes of [def-weil-size-convention]. For a profinite space $P$ (compact Hausdorff and totally disconnected), equip $\\operatorname{Prof}/P$ with finite jointly surjective covering families. For a topological commutative ring $T$, write $R_T(Q\\xrightarrow{a}P)=C(Q,T)$, with pointwise operations and pullback of continuous functions. Use ordinary internal $R_T$-modules [sk-def-sfb-module-objects] and their ordinary uncompleted derived category [def-weil-abstract-derived-category]. Let $\\ell$ be prime and $E/\\mathbf Q_\\ell$ finite with its valuation topology [def-weil-l-adic-coefficient-extension], and suppose $P$ is extremally disconnected. For $a\\in C(P,E)$ let $K_a$ be the actual sheaf kernel of multiplication by $a$ on $R_E$. Explicitly,\n$$K_a(Q\\xrightarrow{b}P)=\\{x\\in C(Q,E):(a\\circ b)x=0\\}.$$\nLet $\\mathcal J$ be any full replete class of $D(\\operatorname{Mod}_{R_E})$ containing every $F[0]$ for which a finite jointly surjective profinite cover of $P$ makes $F$ a finite power of the pulled-back ring $R_E$ (the ranks may vary between cover members). Suppose $\\mathcal J$ contains zero, is closed under all integer shifts, distinguished-triangle extensions, retracts and all small ordinary derived products, and satisfies this strict filtered-colimit condition: for every small filtered diagram $C_i^\\bullet$ of module-sheaf complexes with a common termwise lower bound and $Q(C_i^\\bullet)\\in\\mathcal J$, also $Q(\\varinjlim_iC_i^\\bullet)\\in\\mathcal J$, with the colimit termwise in sheaves and $Q$ localization at quasi-isomorphisms. Then $K_a[0]\\in\\mathcal J$. The kernel is not asserted to be a finite local model or the scalar extension of the kernel on global sections. Empty $P$, $a=0$, and invertible $a$ are included. Closure notions are those of [def-weil-triangulated-subcategory, def-weil-category-product, def-weil-pbc-category-colimit].",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/hemo-richarz-scholbach-constructible-sheaves_arXiv-2305.18131.pdf",
  "place": "Example 4.2 and Remark 6.4 identify the non-lisse rank-one kernel obligation; exact generation reference WANTED. This is an agent-formulated rank-one subproblem, not asserted to be proved by HRS."
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-size-convention",
